  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Mr Kumar’s car travels 120 km/h downhill, 80 km/h on level ground and 60 km/h uphill. It takes him 6 hours to get from Ayetown to Beetown but only 4 hours to return. What is the distance between these two towns?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$400\\text{ km}$.\n\nAdd the outward and return times: every kilometre contributes $\\frac{1}{40}$ hour to the round trip.",
      "worked": "Let $u$, $l$ and $d$ km be the uphill, level and downhill distances from Ayetown to Beetown. Uphill and downhill swap on the return journey.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{u}{60}+\\frac{l}{80}+\\frac{d}{120}&=6\\\\\\frac{u}{120}+\\frac{l}{80}+\\frac{d}{60}&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdding the journey times gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{1}{60}+\\frac{1}{120}\\right)(u+d)+\\frac{2l}{80}&=10\\\\\\frac{u+d}{40}+\\frac{l}{40}&=10\\\\\\frac{u+l+d}{40}&=10\\\\u+l+d&=400\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe distance between the towns is $400\\text{ km}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 88
  },
